"Created and tested `/home/agent/workspace/migration/freeze.sh`:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# freeze.sh — simulates freezing writes during migration by creating\n# a sentinel file (frozen.flag) and printing a confirmation.\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nFLAG_FILE=\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/frozen.flag\"\n\ntouch \"${FLAG_FILE}\"\n\necho \"Writes frozen\"\n```\n\n**Test run:** Ran it and confirmed:\n- Output: `Writes frozen`\n- `frozen.flag` created (empty sentinel file, 0 bytes) in the migration directory\n\nLike the earlier scripts, it resolves paths relative to its own location so it works from any working directory."